# TensionBudget — Web Deployment & ML-Ready Cloud Architecture (Phases W1–W6)

This specification defines the migration of our verified local desktop pipeline (Phases 1–12) into a **modern, secure, multi-user cloud web application** without rewriting any digital signal processing (DSP) logic. The local Python codebase remains the authoritative source of truth and executes directly inside the browser using **Pyodide (WebAssembly)**, while an asynchronous cloud layer on **PostgreSQL** handles user authentication, session logging, and per-user ML personalization.

---

## User Review & Architectural Confirmation
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Zero DSP Rewrites (Source of Truth)**: All existing math in `preprocessing.py`, `scoring.py`, `spectral.py`, and `analytics.py` (using `numpy`/`scipy`) will run unmodified inside Pyodide WebAssembly. We only modify the hardware acquisition boundary: replacing `pyserial` with the browser's native **Web Serial API**.

> [!CAUTION]
> **Raw Signal Persistence Decision (SCOPED POLICY EXCEPTION FOR WEB ONLY)**: In accordance with your confirmation, **raw 500 Hz sEMG streams will NOT be uploaded to the server over the web deployment path**. For browser-based sessions over Web Serial, uploading continuous uncompressed 500 Hz raw signal across residential connections incurs severe network overhead and biological privacy risks. Raw samples exist strictly in temporary browser WebAssembly memory for real-time analysis/visualization and vanish upon tab closure; only discrete 5-minute feature summaries survive server-side.
> **Desktop Path Inviolation**: This is explicitly a scoped privacy exception ONLY for the web path. The local desktop application / `output_logs/` path continues to log and retain full, raw, un-rectified, un-filtered 500 Hz recoverable data exactly as originally mandated by our Phase 1 non-negotiable principle.

> [!NOTE]
> **Symmetrical 500 Hz Hardware Sampling Rate (COM5 & COM6)**: Both Left and Right trapezius channels must operate strictly at **500 Hz (Nyquist = 250 Hz)** to enable uncompromised 20–240 Hz Butterworth bandpass filtering and Welch power spectral fatigue regression across both shoulders. Historical references to 250 Hz test limits on COM5 were due to test firmware prototypes and have been entirely eliminated.

> [!NOTE]
> **Structural Auth vs. Research Data Isolation**: To comply with privacy best practices, authentication (`email`/`password_hash`) is structurally decoupled from biometric research data. Login tables NEVER touch research tables; authentication simply issues an anonymized ID (`user_name` / `subject_id`), which serves as the sole link to physical metadata and ergonomic histories.

> [!TIP]
> **ML-Ready Tabular Design (Flattened Schema + Explicit Missingness)**: To guarantee type safety and native ingestion into ML engines (scikit-learn/XGBoost) without expensive JSON parsing or Parquet over-engineering, `epoch_features` stores every feature as an explicit typed SQL column. Crucially, to prevent conditional MDF/MNF calculations (`NULL` during resting states) from being imputed as `0 Hz` by ML models, we enforce explicit missingness boolean indicators (`mdf_computed_left` / `right`).

