## Complete Runtime Workflow & Data Telemetry Flow

The runtime data collection operates on a clean **3-Stage Telemetry Loop**, precisely mapping physical hardware events to database table insertions at **5-minute intervals** (doubling ML row density over early 10-minute prototypes):

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Workstation User
    participant Browser as Browser UI & Pyodide (Wasm)
    participant API as Cloud API Server
    participant DB as PostgreSQL Database

    note over User, DB: Stage 1: Session Initiation & Personal Calibration
    User->>Browser: Click "Start Recorded Session" & do 5s Shrug Test
    Browser->>Browser: Compute personal baselines: calibration_rms_left & right
    Browser->>API: POST /session/start (user_name, calibration values, processing_version)
    API->>DB: INSERT INTO sessions (user_name, start_time, calibration_rms, processing_version) -> returns session_id

    note over User, DB: Stage 2: Real-Time Monitoring & 5-Minute Periodic Epoch Logging
    loop Real-Time Ergonomic Surveillance (Clock 1: In-Memory 500Hz)
        Browser->>Browser: Stream USB Arduinos via Web Serial & update GUI gauges
        note right of Browser: When Elapsed Time crosses 5-Min boundary (Clock 2):
        Browser->>API: POST /session/log_epoch (session_id, epoch_index, 36 flattened features)
        API->>DB: INSERT INTO epoch_features (session_id, epoch_index, composite_score, mdf_r_squared_left, etc.)
    end

    note over User, DB: Stage 3: Teardown & Final Snapshot
    User->>Browser: Click "Stop Recording" (or close browser tab)
    Browser->>API: POST /session/end (session_id, final_epoch_data)
    API->>DB: INSERT final epoch_features row & UPDATE sessions SET end_time = now()
```

