### 1. Tier 1: The Privacy & Identity Firewall
- **`auth_users`**: Holds sensitive login authentication (`email`, `password_hash`). Its sole purpose is to authenticate the user and issue an anonymized ID (`user_name` or UUID).
- **`user_profiles` (Canonical Research Vault)**: Keyed strictly by `user_name` (Table 1 in `cloud_schema.py`). Contains NO emails or passwords.
  - **Biological Attributes**: `birth_date` (TEXT/DATE), `gender_sex` (TEXT), `weight_kg` (REAL), `height_cm` (REAL), `updated_at` (REAL/TIMESTAMP).
  - **Dynamic Age Computation**: Computed dynamically at query time via SQL: `EXTRACT(YEAR FROM AGE(birth_date::date))`.
  - **Dynamic BMI Computation**: When weight and height exist, Body Mass Index ($BMI = \frac{\text{weight in kg}}{(\text{height in m})^2}$) is evaluated dynamically in SQL: `ROUND(weight_kg / POWER(height_cm / 100.0, 2), 2)`.

### 2. Tier 2: The Working Session & Personal Baseline
- **`sessions`**: Created when a user begins a monitoring sitting (Table 2 in `cloud_schema.py`). Linked upward to Tier 1 via `user_name`.
  - **Calibration Storage**: Captures the exact physical baseline from their initial 5-second shoulder shrug test: `calibration_rms_left` (REAL) and `calibration_rms_right` (REAL). Storing this here ensures every historical session permanently records the baseline sensitivity that governed its scores.
  - **Processing Version Tagging**: Captures `processing_version` (e.g. `'phase11_edge_padding'` or `'legacy_constant_padding'`) to prevent numerical corruption during pooled ML training across disparate signal processing iterations.

### 3. Tier 3: The 5-Minute Longitudinal Feature Logs
All analytical tables point upward to `sessions(session_id)` via Foreign Keys (`FK`), creating an unbroken chain connecting every single 5-minute snapshot back to the exact shrug calibration and physical subject profile:
- **`epoch_features` (Canonical Wide Feature Matrix)**: Table 3 in `cloud_schema.py`. Exactly ONE row is added every **5 minutes** from session start to session end, doubling ML row density over early prototypes.
  - Complete Column Set: `feature_id`, `session_id` (FK), `epoch_index`, `elapsed_minutes`, `composite_score`, `eindex_live_left/right`, `eindex_cumulative_left/right`, `short_suma_penalty_left/right`, `total_suma_bursts_left/right`, `gap_frequency_left/right`, `apdf_10_left/right`, `apdf_50_left/right`, `apdf_90_left/right`, `asymmetry_index_ai`, `asymmetry_penalty_applied`, `mdf_hz_left/right`, `mnf_hz_left/right`, `fatigue_slope_left/right`, **`mdf_r_squared_left/right` (Quality Diagnostic)**, **`n_windows_left/right` (Buffer Verification)**, **`mdf_computed_left/right` (Explicit Missingness Boolean)**, and `is_fatiguing_left/right`.
- **`self_reports`**: Logs timestamped user subjective perceived exertion ratings (RPE 1–10) during the working session.
- **`alert_events`**: Captures asynchronous real-time browser alarms fired when posture asymmetry or muscle fatigue exceed tolerance during active GUI tracking.
- **`v_ml_training_pairs` (SQL VIEW)**: Automatically joins Tier 1 (`user_profiles` demographic features), Tier 2 (`sessions` shrug baseline and `processing_version`), and Tier 3 (`epoch_features` + matched `self_reports`), exporting clean $X \rightarrow Y$ training DataFrames directly to `pandas.read_sql()`.

